# django-query-doctor ignore rules.
#
# taggit's TaggableManager.add() issues one INSERT per tag via an internal
# get_or_create() loop on the through model (TaggedItem). This happens inside
# the third-party django-taggit library, not in our code, and cannot be
# bulk-ified without bypassing taggit's public API -- doing so would lose
# the m2m_changed signals and TAGGIT_CASE_INSENSITIVE handling it provides.
# Accepted as a known limitation rather than worked around.
ignore:write_n_plus_one:articles/serializers.py
